1. Docker Basics 🐳
Docker ek containerization platform hai jo application aur uski dependencies ko ek container me pack karta hai.

> Docker ka kaam:
Application ko run karna
Environment same rakhna (Development → Testing → Production)
Fast deployment

> Example:
Aapne Node.js application banayi.
Docker us app ko container me pack kar deta hai, jisse wo kisi bhi machine par bina issue ke run ho sakti hai.
Docker = Container banane aur chalane ka tool

2. Kubernetes Basics ☸️
Kubernetes (K8s) ek Container Orchestration Tool hai.
Jab bahut saare Docker containers hote hain, unko manage karne ke liye Kubernetes use hota hai.

> Kubernetes ka kaam:
Containers ko manage karna
Auto Scaling
Load Balancing
Self-Healing
Deployment Management

> Example:
Aapke paas 100 Docker containers hain.
Unhe manually manage karna mushkil hai.
Kubernetes automatically sab containers ko manage karega.
Kubernetes = Containers ka Manager


3. Container vs Orchestration
Docker (Container)	          Kubernetes (Orchestration)
Container create karta hai. 
Containers manage karta hai.
Single application run kar sakta hai.	
Multiple applications manage karta hai.
Lightweight	Large-scale management
Packaging tool	Management tool

> Easy Trick:
🏠 Docker = Ghar banana
👨‍💼 Kubernetes = Society Manager jo sab ghar manage karta hai

4. Scaling & Management
> Docker Scaling
Agar traffic badh gaya to manually naye containers chalane padenge.
// docker run app
// docker run app
// docker run app
Sab manually karna padega.

> Kubernetes Scaling
Kubernetes automatic scaling karta hai.
kubectl scale deployment app --replicas=5
Ya traffic badhne par khud bhi containers badha sakta hai.

> Kubernetes Features:
✅ Auto Scaling
✅ Load Balancing
✅ Self-Healing
✅ Rolling Updates
✅ Auto Restart

